{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cg5zGfJXDsMJzsnkWhnPN","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The ratchet gate is green (`ratchet-gate day16`, exit 0). There were no worker proposals today, so everything below comes from the GM-confirmed results.\n\n1. **Warmups (morse-hex):** day 16's codec is Morse code spelling the hex digits of the UTF-8 sentence. I added it to `lib/warmups_codecs.DAYS` as day 16; the encoder reproduces the GM's blob byte-for-byte. I also added a branch in `lib.decode.decode_chunk` so the decoded sentence wins over the raw hex reading. It decodes the single and both Time Trial cases to their confirmed slugs, and there's a new check in `tests/test_day7_fixes.py`.\n2. **Metadata (`email.message_id`):** the new verified extractor is `lib/meta/eml.py:message_id`. It returns the Message-ID verbatim with the angle brackets kept, as confirmed on the single, the Time Trial and all 5 Mastery sets. I removed `(\"eml\",\"message_id\")` from the prebuilt `FIELDS`. The GM calls the format `email` while the prebuilt module uses `eml`, so `resolve()` now maps one name to the other; the rest of the e-mail fields stay unconfirmed. The two wrong spellings from the single (no brackets, and `\"none\"`) are in `EMAIL_MESSAGE_ID_REJECTED` in `lib/knowledge.py`.\n3. **Metadata speed fix:** the first gate run failed on the 1 s lane-solver limit (1.04–1.09 s on Mastery cases from day 15 and day 16). The cause was older code: `lib.meta.parse_field` rebuilt about 68k regexes per run. It now compiles them once, which takes the case from about 1.0 s to 0.4 s with identical answers.\n4. **Scripting (batch \"expansion\" questions):** on day 16 the GM labelled the expansion form from the reconstruction statement alone, even on attempts without `run_for_time` set (18/18 confirmed on the single and Time Trial; the old `delayed` answer for a `%`-join was rejected). I recorded this in the expansion rule in `lib/playbook.py` and in a new `BATCH_EXPANSION_STATEMENT_SINCE` constant in `lib/knowledge.py`. The 5 Mastery `error:exec` results were all \"local hb_timed timed out\", a harness problem rather than a lib one, so nothing went into lib for them.\n5. **Rejected / not merged:** binary and mobile passed first try by reusing earlier solvers and added no new codec, so nothing was merged. I did not register a verified entry pointing into `lib/meta/prebuilt/` as the task asked, because `test_meta_lane` forbids it; that's why the extractor lives in `lib/meta/eml.py` instead. The metadata Time Trial and Mastery needed a generalize only because the day solver lacked the synthesis-order field, which `lib.meta.synthesis` already covers, so nothing new was added for it."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":198,"cache_read_input_tokens":109562,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":198},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e3be7344-0731-4df8-a19b-60d7e80de6a6","uuid":"142c2ae0-741b-42fb-848b-e36498677de6","timestamp":"2026-10-16T13:23:27.634Z","request_id":"req_011Cg5zGek2xY9LQQm1SX6qS"}
